    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1644">

                <pb facs="1042" n="926" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg926"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 511.4A1/1460.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister of the
                            Netherlands to the Secretary of
                        State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 2324.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the Netherlands</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-04-27">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 27, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Secretary of State</hi>: In continuation of my
                    note No. 1740 of January 27 last and forwarding to your excellency herewith 4
                    copies of a list giving the names of the Powers that have signed the Opium
                    Convention, I have the honor to inform you that the Convention has been signed: <list>
                        <label>1.</label>
                        <item>By Great Britain for the Leeward Islands January 30, 1914; for British
                            Guiana and British Honduras February 11, 1914; for the Government of the
                            South African Union March 11, 1914; for Zanzibar, North Rhodesia, and
                            North Basutoland, the protectorate <pb facs="1043" n="927"
                                xml:id="pg927"/> of Bechuanaland and Swasiland March 28, 1914; for
                            the colony of Barbados April 4, 1914; and for Mauritius and its
                            dependencies April 8, 1914.</item>
                        <label>2.</label>
                        <item>By Bulgaria, March 2, 1914.</item>
                        <label>3.</label>
                        <item>By Uruguay, March 9, 1914.</item>
                    </list>
                </p>
                <p>The Convention has been ratified by China. I embrace this opportunity to renew
                    [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">W. L. F. C. de Rappard</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
